is deletion in turn can happen only for data that has been marked for deletion.Note  Your on-premise communication system needs to fulfill specific requirements for the Marked for Deletion indicator to be available. If these requirements are not met and the Marked for Deletion indicator accordingly isn't available, SAP Advanced Financial Closing will keep a reference to the data until the communication system fulfills the requirements and the data can be marked for deletion.For more information about the requirements, see System-Dependent Feature Availability.  More information:  How to Delete Task List Templates and Task Lists  System-Dependent Feature Availability    App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Action: If you're using SAP Advanced Financial Closing with a connected on-premise system, check whether your communication system fulfills the requirements to mark data used by SAP Advanced Financial Closing for deletion.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-05\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3058 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional Generate Task List Option\nDescription: You can now generate a task list using the new Generate Task List button on the header of a task list template. It's still possible to generate a task list from the Templates tab.  More information:  How to Generate and Release Task Lists  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-05\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3059 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Business Feature Validation\nDescription: If tasks in an on-premise communication system are assigned to a business feature (switch) in the communication system, the state of this business feature is now also checked when you copy a task list template.  If the current business feature state renders a task invalid for the specific use case, the template is copied without the invalid tasks.  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-05\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3060 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Improvement to Copy Folders Dialog for Organizational Units\nDescription: In the Copy Folders dialog for organizational units, you can now use a quick filter to decide which target organizational units are displayed. You have the following options:  All  Not Existing Below System Folder  Existing Below System Folder    Additionally, a new column shows you whether an organizational unit already exists below the system folder.  More information:  How to Copy Folders  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-05\nValid as Of: 2024-04-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3791 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Number Ranges in Company/Trading Partner Profile\nDescription: You can now configure Number Ranges in a company/trading partner profile.  See:     Creating a Company Profile and a Subsidiary    Creating a Trading Partner Profile  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-04\nValid as Of: 2023-12-04\nVersion: 2310\n\n--- Record 3792 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Cloud Integration: 6.43.*  Increment: 2310  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-04\nValid as Of: 2023-12-04\nVersion: 2310\n\n--- Record 3793 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tradacoms Type System\nDescription: You can now use Tradacoms type system in your B2B scenarios.  See:     Creating a Company Profile and a Subsidiary    Creating a Trading Partner Profile  Trading Partner Agreement    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-04\nValid as Of: 2023-12-04\nVersion: 2310\n\n--- Record 3794 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Forms and Approvals\nDescription: You can select whether form or approval recipients can forward the task to another user. For more information, see Configure a Form to Start a Process.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3795 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Store - New Content Packages\nDescription: A new set of 23 content packages, 12 Business Content and 11 Learning Content have been added to the Store during Nov-Dec 2023. We have also made some fixes in the existing content packages.  These content packages are tailored to different lines of business such as IT, Sales, Services, Sourcing, Finance, and Procurement.  SAP S/4HANA Business Content:  Mass Purchase Order Confirmations.  Contract Employee End Date Extension.  Mass Automation of Accrual Posting.  Mass Maintenance of Source Lists (4TK).  Mass Maintenance of Cost Centers.  https://api.sap.com/package/eu10.storecontentdevacc.nonrepairablepartautorecordingwithgoodsmovement/overview.  Automate Mass Upload of GL Journal Entries.  Automatic Picking of Outbound Deliveries.  Automate Posting of Goods Receipt.  Mass Clearing of GL, Customer and Supplier Open Items.    SAP S/4HANA Learning Content:  In-App Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Scope Item J58 (6PR).  In-App Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Scope Items J45 and 18J (6PQ).  In-App Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Scope Items J60 and 1NT (6PT).  In-App Configuration for SAP S4HANA Cloud Scope item J59 (6PS).  In-App Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Scope Items 1LQ (6PP).  In-App Configuration for SAP S4HANA Cloud Scope Item 1F1 2LH 2V7 BD9 (6PE).  Mass Upload of Business Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud (6PX).    Other Learning Contents:  Automate Microsoft Office 365 applications.  Manage calendar events with Microsoft Office 365.  Innovation Idea Process.    Updated Content:  Ariba Purchase Requisition Approval.  Documents Centric Approvals Process.  Note  The old version of the Document-Centric Approval Process has been deprecated. The new version has been released with a name change, as indicated in the Updated Content section.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-05\nValid as Of: 2023-12-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3796 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: OpenID Connect Authentication\nDescription: OpenID Connect (OIDC) authentication with an Identity Authentication tenant is now available as a Beta feature for your applications in the Neo environment.   See OpenID Connect (OIDC) Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Beta\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-30\nValid as Of: 2023-11-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3797 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of Weak Client Certificate Chains\nDescription: As originally announced on May 18, 2023 and November 2, 2023, weak client certificate chains have been deprecated for the region eu20 in order to harden security standards.   Accordingly, the OpenSSL security has been raised to level 2, resulting in weak certificates or certificate chains no longer being accepted by the platform. For more information and a full definition of security level 2, see https://www.openssl.org/docs/man3.0", " Client Certificate Chains\nDescription: As originally announced on May 18, 2023 and November 2, 2023, weak client certificate chains have been deprecated for the region eu20 in order to harden security standards.   Accordingly, the OpenSSL security has been raised to level 2, resulting in weak certificates or certificate chains no longer being accepted by the platform. For more information and a full definition of security level 2, see https://www.openssl.org/docs/man3.0/man3/SSL_CTX_set_security_level.html#DEFAULT-CALLBACK-BEHAVIOUR.   Note that this change only affects client certificates. If you do not use client certificates or mTLS to authenticate with the platform, you are not affected.   For more details on the command, see 3333978 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-30\nValid as Of: 2023-11-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3798 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Command Line Tools\nDescription: You can now have access to the following command line tools: make and helm to execute scripts in a fully isolated Linux environment. See ExecuteScript Version 1 and ExecuteScript Version 2.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-30\nValid as Of: 2023-11-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3799 ---\nComponent: Custom Domain Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Alert Notifications\nDescription: You can now receive alert notifications if there are critical issues in your custom domains, such as expiring certificates or deprecated cipher suites. For more information, see Alert Notifications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-30\nValid as Of: 2023-11-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3800 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP Fiori UI5 Theme: Horizon\nDescription: With this release, the following themes are supported in the Document Management Service, Application Option.    Morning Horizon    Evening Horizon  Horizon High Contrast White  Horizon High Contrast Black    To activate the theme, go to your user profile and choose Settings. Then, select Appearance and choose your preferred theme from the options available.  For more information about managing your settings, see Personalize the Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-30\nValid as Of: 2023-11-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 281 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Print Queue Administrator Integration\nDescription: You can now create and delete print queues directly using APIs without the need to enter the Maintain Print Queues app. You can do so using the communication scenario SAP_COM_0A86.  See SAP_COM_0A86.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 282 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: RAP Factory Actions\nDescription: RAP factory actions now return the http status 201 instead of 200 in case of a successful OData V4 response.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-07\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 283 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Redesign of Fiori Space and Page Templates for the Custom Code Migration App\nDescription: The Custom Code Migration Fiori app has been split up into two separate tiles. There is now the Analyze Custom Code app for the custom code analysis use case and the Custom Code Migration app for the migration to SAP S/4HANA use case.  If you're using the business role Quality Manager - Software Development, you'll find the Analyze Custom Code app. If you're using the business role Project Manager - IT, you'll find the Custom Code Migration app.  See Custom Code Analysis. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 284 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Reduce Footprint of Business Configuration Maintenance Objects\nDescription: With the existing RAP generator for business configuration maintenance objects, you can easily generate all development objects that are required for a configuration object. Since the number of objects is still quite large, optimizations in the RAP programming model have been implemented that reduce the number of required development objects and make them easier for a developer to manage.  For more information, see Creating Business Configuration Maintenance Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 285 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Reduction of Technical Downtime for Hotfix Collection Imports\nDescription: A new update procedure reduces the technical downtime during the installation of hotfix collections in a non-development SAP BTP ABAP environment system. These new procedures split the update process into three phases: a preparation phase, a short takeover phase, and a postprocessing phase. The preparation phase installs the updated software version into a shadow layer of the system. The takeover phase switches to the new software version. As part of the takeover, running ABAP applications are terminated and new sessions will start on the new software version. This takeover induces a short downtime of the system in the area of seconds up to a minute. Finalization tasks and clean-up steps run in the postprocessing phase. Both the preparation phase as well as the postprocessing phase run in the background during uptime of the system. Some lifecycle management activities, like the import of transports or tenant creation, are blocked during the preparation phase. These downtime improvements become effective with the first hotfix collection update of the 2508 release.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 286 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Reduction of Technical Downtime for Release Upgrades\nDescription: New upgrade procedures reduce the technical downtime during the installation of new releases in a non-development SAP BTP ABAP environment system. These new procedures split the upgrade process into three phases: a preparation phase, a short takeover phase, and a postprocessing phase. The preparation phase installs the new platform release into a shadow layer of the system. The takeover phase switches to the new platform version. The switch to the new platform release happens within a shortened downtime of 20 to 40 minutes. Finalization tasks and clean-up steps run in the postprocessing phase. Both the preparation phase as well as the postprocessing phase run in the background during uptime of the system. Some lifecycle management activities, like the import of transports or tenant creation, are blocked during the preparation phase. These new procedures were already applied during recent upgrades, but will become even more beneficial with the planned system-specific announcement of precise technical downtime. In the first phase, we provide this feature to production systems running on 4 or more HANA Consumption Units.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 287 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 4 (which is used for the standard upgrade), SAPUI5 version 1.136.4 is used for the", "Type: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 287 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 4 (which is used for the standard upgrade), SAPUI5 version 1.136.4 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2025 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 288 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: Manage Launchpad Spaces and Pages: Redesign and Renaming\nDescription: In the SAP Fiori launchpad, both the Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages apps were redesigned. We adapted the overview pages to enhance working with spaces and space templates, as well as with pages and page templates. \"Predefined\" and \"SAP-Delivered\" were renamed to \"Templates\" to ensure consistent terminology between these apps, the Maintain Business Roles app and the ABAP Development Tools for space and page templates.  See Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 289 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: New Layout for Launchpad Shell Bar and Menus\nDescription: The layout of the SAP Fiori launchpad shell bar, user menu, notifications list, navigation menu and user settings was changed according to the current SAP Design System. The user experience was harmonized across different SAP products. The navigation menu was enhanced and is now part of the shell bar. It now offers access to My Home, Favorite Apps, My Spaces and All Spaces.   The sorting options in the notifications list were simplified. In addition, there is a new button to directly open the settings from here. The order of entries in the user menu as well as in the user settings has been adapted.  See User Menu, Shell and Shell Bar and Working with Notifications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 290 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Server-Sent Events in ABAP HTTP\nDescription: The ABAP HTTP client and server now support server-sent events (SSE). Which allows a server to send parts of the body of the response to the client without the client having to actively request them. After being sent by the server, the client can fetch them as they become available.  For more information, see Enabling Server-Sent Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n", "--- Record 2421 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating CDS Aspects in ABAP CDS Syntax\nDescription: You can now create CDS aspects to store field definitions and calculations, such as CDS expressions, in order to reuse them in other data definitions.  See Creating CDS Aspects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2422 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating Logical External Schemas\nDescription: You can now create logical external schemas that can be used in combination with external entities for establishing outbound SQL access.  See Working with Logical External Schemas.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2423 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Display Warnings Sent by SAP HANA\nDescription: When debugging a development object in which ABAP Managed Database Procedures (AMDP) are nested, the AMDP Debugger now displays warnings that are sent by the SAP HANA database.  See Stepping in AMDP Debugger.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2424 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Field Extension Wizard\nDescription: You can now use the field extension wizard to create extension fields.  See Generating Extension Fields.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2425 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Generating an ABAP CDS Provider Model\nDescription: The Generate ABAP Repository Objects Wizard creates ABAP development objects based on the Core Schema Notation model workbench object. It generates DDIC tables, CDS views, metadata extensions, and service definitions.  See Generating an ABAP CDS Provider Model with the Generate ABAP Repository Objects Wizard.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2426 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Maintain Baseline in the Custom Code Migration App\nDescription: You can now use the feature of adding findings to the baseline in the Custom Code Migration app.  See Custom Code Migration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2427 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: New Feature Explorer Tour for RAP Business Object Tooling\nDescription: The new RAP BO tools tour has been added to the Feature Explorer. The tour allows you to learn more about the different features that are available for RAP BO development.  See Feature Explorer.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2428 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Opening Non-Native-Integrated Development Objects\nDescription: If you open an ABAP development object that is not native-integrated in Eclipse, it will now be opened in a new fallback editor in ADT. This editor shows, for example, the information that is usually displayed in the Properties view or the source code in a read-only preview.  See Opening Non-Native-Integrated Development Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2429 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Planned Decommissioning Date for Deprecated Objects\nDescription: For formerly released but meanwhile deprecated local APIs, the system now shows their planned decommissioning date. If SAP has no concrete plans to change the state of an object to decommissioned, the date is not set, and the priorities of the corresponding ATC check results (developer extensibility) and rework tasks (key user extensibility) are lower than for objects with a planned decommissioning date. This will help you to prioritize the rework of custom objects that use deprecated APIs.  See Deprecation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business:", " plans to change the state of an object to decommissioned, the date is not set, and the priorities of the corresponding ATC check results (developer extensibility) and rework tasks (key user extensibility) are lower than for objects with a planned decommissioning date. This will help you to prioritize the rework of custom objects that use deprecated APIs.  See Deprecation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2430 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Schedule Custom Code Analysis\nDescription: Through the Schedule Custom Code Analysis app, you can now schedule projects created in the Custom Code Migration app as application jobs. With this functionality, the analyses can be performed once or periodically. The Schedule Custom Code Analysis app is available to all users that have access to the Custom Code Migration app.  See Schedule Custom Code Analysis.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n", "--- Record 1581 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Configurations API – Read Single Characteristics\nDescription: There is a new endpoint called GET /api/v2/configurations/{configurationId}/items/{itemId}/characteristics used to read the details of one or more characteristics of an item.   Action: If the UI of the consuming application allows it, it is recommended to always read the configuration results during interactive configuration without the possible values of characteristics. This can be achieved by using the parameter $select omitting the parameter value possibleValue when creating or reading a configuration. Only when the user clicks on a UI element, like a dropdown list box, that requires to render the possible values on the UI, the possible values should be read for that characteristic using the new endpoint. This will improve performance especially when AVC Forwarding is enabled.   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1582 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Staged Deployment Strategy\nDescription: There is a new staged deployment strategy for the Variant Configuration service starting with the 2502 release. New software releases used to be deployed to all customer tenants at the same time. We will continue to do that for our administration UI and our Administration service, but for the configuration and pricing services we will first deploy the 2502 release only to all non-productive tenants (including the partner tenants) on January 22, 2025 and only two weeks later, on February 5, 2025 we will also deploy it to the productive tenants.  Action: It is recommended to make yourself familiar with the release dates on our product page. Review the changes in the Pre-Production version of the documentation that will be published on January 22, and use the given two weeks to test the new release in your non-productive tenants and process the actions of the recommended or required changes that are announced here in the release notes.  See: Release Schedule and Dates.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1583 ---\nComponent: Application for Data Replication and Administration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Actions - Remote Subscription Exception Display\nDescription: The update mechanism for displaying errors relating to the SDI DP Agent was not working properly. This led to instances in which the error was shown only for a few seconds. This issue has been corrected\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1584 ---\nComponent: Application for Data Replication and Administration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Delta Replication Alert for SAP CALM\nDescription: The alert for a too high number of deltas is now also sent to SAP Cloud Application Lifecycle Monitoring – Integration Monitoring.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-12\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1585 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Component for SAP Support Updated\nDescription: In the Help Center topic View Data in a Datastore, the component you should use when asking SAP Support to activate View Data functionality for you has been updated to LOD-HCI-DS-OPS.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-22\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: 1.0.11.55\n\n--- Record 1586 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription: The microservice now supports parsing point of reference data in Spanish South America countries. See the Point of Reference description in Extended Address for more information\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1587 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Kyma runtime system maintenance\nDescription: We are upgrading the Kyma runtime management in our Kyma Control Plane. During this upgrade, the following minor adjustment will be applied to your Kubernetes cluster:  ClusterRoleBindings of administrators will be temporarily duplicated. This will not affect the access to your cluster. The redundant ClusterRoleBindings will be removed in a post action.  The upgrade process starts in calendar week 04/2025 and will be completed in week 06/2025.  Please note that:    The upgrade is a zero-downtime maintenance.  No actions are required from your side.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-17\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1588 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.31.0\nDescription: The new", "owntime maintenance.  No actions are required from your side.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-17\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1588 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.31.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:  Metrics: Improved MetricPipeline defaulting of inputs (#1712).  Traces and Metrics: Update to OTel Collector 0.116.0 (#1071).   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-08\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1589 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production - Base Calculations Include Current Percentage Step\nDescription: In scenarios where a percentage condition spans multiple counters within the same step range in the pricing procedure, the condition base used not to be dynamically adjusted to account for the cumulative effect of prior conditions. Instead, all counters for the condition type used to use the original base amount. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1590 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production - Standard Requirement Formula 58\nDescription: Support standard requirement formula 58 that returns true if the accounting indicator (KOMP-BEMOT) is not initial.  See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_ade768380589286cfe5ad82e2638438fd642a2e1879241a10668bfd1721d856a_v2"}